      "question": "What if my anesthesiologist is out of network?",
      "answer": "If you used most types of private insurance and the anesthesiologist treated you at an in-network hospital, hospital outpatient department or ambulatory surgical center, the No Surprises Act protects you from unexpected out-of-network bills in most cases. CMS says anesthesiologists are not allowed to ask you to sign a notice and consent form. Compare the bill with your EOB Patient Balance and call your plan if the bill is higher."
    },
    {
      "question": "Can I be billed more than in-network rates at an in-network hospital?",
